karte hain, jahan count current consecutive ones ko count karega aur max1 ab tak ki maximum consecutive ones ki count 
store karega. Uske baad for(int i=0; i<n; i++) loop se array ke har element ko traverse karte hain. Agar nums[i] == 1 
hota hai, toh count++ karke consecutive ones ki count increase karte hain aur max1 = max(max1, count) se maximum count 
update karte hain. Agar element 1 nahi hota, toh count = 0 kar dete hain, kyunki consecutive sequence break ho gayi hai 
aur next sequence ki counting zero se start hogi. Finally, return max1 se maximum consecutive ones ki count return kar 
dete hain. For example, agar array {1,1,0,1,1,1,0,1} hai, toh consecutive ones ke groups ki counts 2, 3 aur 1 hain, 
isliye output 3 hoga. Is approach ki Time Complexity O(n) aur Auxiliary Space Complexity O(1) hai, kyunki hum array 
